@id("close-workorder-main-with-person-approval")
permit (principal, action == Drupe::Action::"MaintData___close_workorder", resource)
when { context.input.site_id == "MAIN" }
when temporal {
  formerly within 1h Drupe::Action::"Dorvane___get_approval"::response{
    eventResource: resource,
    input.site_id: context.input.site_id,
    input.wonum: context.input.wonum,
    output.decision: Drupe::Dorvane___get_approval_Output_decision::"ACCEPTED",
    output.approver_kind: Drupe::Dorvane___get_approval_Output_approver_kind::"PERSON"
  }
};

// Read-only lookups. The Dorvane approval lookup must be permitted, or it is
// never recorded as a response and can never confirm an approval.
@id("allow-read-only-lookups")
permit (
  principal,
  action in [
    Drupe::Action::"Dorvane___get_approval",
    Drupe::Action::"Lunvick___get_approval",
    Drupe::Action::"MaintData___get_workorder",
    Drupe::Action::"MaintData___list_workorders",
    Drupe::Action::"MaintData___get_my_assigned_workorders",
    Drupe::Action::"MaintData___get_workorder_tasks",
    Drupe::Action::"MaintData___get_workorder_costs",
    Drupe::Action::"MaintData___get_workorder_actuals_vs_planned",
    Drupe::Action::"MaintData___get_workorder_kpis",
    Drupe::Action::"MaintData___get_schedule_calendar",
    Drupe::Action::"MaintData___get_failure_codes"
  ],
  resource
);

// The agent must never approve work orders itself.
@id("never-approve")
forbid (principal, action == Drupe::Action::"MaintData___approve_workorder", resource);
```

Design choices:

- **Approval source:** Only the Dorvane approval lookup counts as proof of approval. Its output is a closed enum, so `ACCEPTED` and `PERSON` can be matched exactly. The Lunvick lookup returns free-form strings with no declared vocabulary, so it is permitted as a read-only lookup but cannot satisfy the close condition.
- **Enum literals:** I wrote the enum matches as entity literals (for example `Drupe::Dorvane___get_approval_Output_decision::"ACCEPTED"`) because the output fields are typed as enum entities. The reference only shows string literals in output patterns, so this syntax is untested against your validator.
- **Closing:** Only closes at site `MAIN` are permitted, and only when a completed Dorvane lookup in the last hour returned an accepted decision by a person. The lookup must also match the same work order and site.
- **Self-approval:** `approve_workorder` is never permitted and is explicitly forbidden. `generate_work_order`, `update_workorder`, `assign_technician` and `cancel_workorder` get no permit, so they are denied by default.

